We are working with the following tables: guser(uid int primary key, uname varchar); category(cid int primary key, cname varchar); gift(id int primary key, descr varchar, price int, cID int references category(cid)); contribution(uid int primary key references guser(uid), amount int not null); preference(uid int references guser(uid), cid int references category(cid), porder int not null check (1<=porder and porder<=3), primary key (uid, cid, porder)); A user preference order (porder) of 1 is the option the user favors most; 2 is the “next” preference order, and 3 is the least favored preference order. If a user u put a category c first in her preference order, we view this as a support score of 3 (the max).